   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">I have a sample Shiny server running on my local machine, but I want to use the directory to host multiple apps. One app at a time seems just fine, but errors with the directory structure is as follows:</span><br><div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;white-space:pre\">/ShinyApp\r\n    /www\r\n        index.html\r\n        /hello\r\n            ui.R\r\n            server.R</span><span style=\"font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;white-space:pre\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">When I go to http://mycomputername:port, the index.html file shows. Going to http://mycomputername:port/hello returns:</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;white-space:pre\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;white-space:pre\">    ERROR: cannot open the connection</span><span style=\"font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;white-space:pre\"><br></span></div><div><p style=\"margin-top:0.357143em;margin-bottom:0.357143em;font-size:14px;line-height:1.42857em;font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Why is this?</p><p style=\"margin-top:0.357143em;margin-bottom:0.357143em;font-size:14px;line-height:1.42857em;font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">The ui.R and server.R files are from <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shiny-server/tree/master/samples/sample-apps/hello\" style=\"color:rgb(0,121,211)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shiny-server/tree/master/samples/sample-apps/hello&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393837017000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3QlB7ovjIAhg_uGuoZ56FN\">this example</a>.</p><p style=\"margin-top:0.357143em;margin-bottom:0.357143em;font-size:14px;line-height:1.42857em;font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">The actual (Linux) server I want to run this on is taking it just fine. I am running this on Windows 7 via</p><p style=\"margin-top:0.357143em;margin-bottom:0.357143em;font-size:14px;line-height:1.42857em;font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-top:0.357143em;margin-bottom:0.357143em;font-size:14px;line-height:1.42857em;font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace;line-height:20px;white-space:pre\">    R -e &quot;shiny:runApp()&quot;</span><br></p><p style=\"margin-top:0.357143em;margin-bottom:0.357143em;font-size:14px;line-height:1.42857em;font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace;line-height:20px;white-space:pre\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0.357143em;margin-bottom:0.357143em;font-size:14px;line-height:1.42857em;font-family:verdana,arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:20px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">on the directory in question</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace;line-height:20px;white-space:pre\"><br></span></p></div></div>"
    ]
