  {
   "id": "mJ2SBgrZAwAJ",
   "from": "Erik Westlund",
   "author": "5ab11db47365dff1",
   "date": "2016-05-03T15:18:41Z",
   "subject": "Re: Local Shiny app -- subdirectory issue",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">ui.R and server.R should be located in the root directory (/Shinyapp) <div><br></div><div><br></div><div>You can access what&#39;s in the /www directory because Shiny Server remaps assets in the /www to the root when a server request is made</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>For example, I have an app where</div><div><br></div><div>ui.R</div><div>server.R are in the root</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>I have a custom style sheet that I load through ui.R.  It&#39;s placed in:</div><div><br></div><div>www/assets/custom.css</div><div><br></div><div>But the link to it is <a href=\"http://shiny.app/assets/custom.css\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.app/assets/custom.css&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393837017000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3dDQy-9m5OjEqIM02YPX4P\">shiny.app/assets/custom.css</a></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Erik</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, May 3, 2016 at 10:16 AM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">webm...@tempest-tech.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
